{"id":"camino-portugues-coastal","title":"Camino Portugués, coastal way","who":"Classic route · about half of all Portuguese Camino pilgrims in 2025","when":"Best April–June and September–October","vehicle":"On foot, 12–15 days","kind":"walk","color":"#1d4ed8","summary":"Porto to Santiago de Compostela along the Atlantic: boardwalks, beaches and fishing towns through northern Portugal, a ferry over the Minho into Galicia, then the bays of Vigo and Pontevedra before joining the central route to the cathedral. Flat, social and easy to plan, with albergues every few kilometres.","sources":[{"label":"Julie Dawn Fox: the Litoral Way (2025 walk)","url":"https://juliedawnfox.com/litoral-way-coastal-camino-portugal/"},{"label":"Stingy Nomads: Coastal Route stages (2026 guide)","url":"https://stingynomads.com/portuguese-coastal-camino-stages/"}],"approximate":"Usual stages from recent guides and reports; the path follows the marked way only approximately.","km":271,"bbox":[-8.8865,41.1429,-8.5458,42.8805],"stops":[{"name":"Porto","place":"Sé do Porto, Porto","at":[41.1428,-8.6112],"text":"Credential stamped at the cathedral, then down to the Douro and out along the river to the sea at Foz.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Porto%2C_S%C3%A9_do_Porto_%289%29.jpg/500px-Porto%2C_S%C3%A9_do_Porto_%289%29.jpg","page":"Porto Cathedral","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Porto%2C_S%C3%A9_do_Porto_%289%29.jpg","credit":"Laszlo Daroczy from Miskolc, Hungary","license":"CC BY 2.0"}},{"name":"Vila do Conde","place":"Vila do Conde, Portugal","at":[41.354,-8.7435],"text":"Boardwalks over the dunes past Matosinhos and Labruge to a town of shipyards and a long aqueduct.","source":{"label":"Julie Dawn Fox (2025)","url":"https://juliedawnfox.com/litoral-way-coastal-camino-portugal/"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Vila_do_Conde.JPG/500px-Vila_do_Conde.JPG","page":"Vila do Conde","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vila_do_Conde.JPG","credit":"PedroPVZ","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Esposende","place":"Esposende, Portugal","at":[41.5315,-8.7793],"text":"Past the windmills of Apúlia on the beach and into the Cávado estuary.","source":{"label":"Julie Dawn Fox (2025)","url":"https://juliedawnfox.com/litoral-way-coastal-camino-portugal/"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/C%C3%A2mara_de_Esposende.jpg/500px-C%C3%A2mara_de_Esposende.jpg","page":"Esposende","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:C%C3%A2mara_de_Esposende.jpg","credit":"Joseolgon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Viana do Castelo","place":"Viana do Castelo, Portugal","at":[41.6935,-8.8283],"text":"Over the Eiffel-era bridge into Viana, watched by the basilica of Santa Luzia on its hill.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Viana_do_Castelo_%2815727153460%29.jpg/500px-Viana_do_Castelo_%2815727153460%29.jpg","page":"Viana do Castelo","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Viana_do_Castelo_%2815727153460%29.jpg","credit":"Lucas Martínez Farrapeira","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0"}},{"name":"Caminha","place":"Caminha, Portugal","at":[41.8492,-8.7727],"text":"The last Portuguese town. Pilgrims cross the Minho estuary by small ferry or taxi-boat to A Guarda.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Caminha_e_Camposancos.JPG/500px-Caminha_e_Camposancos.JPG","page":"Caminha","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Caminha_e_Camposancos.JPG","credit":"HombreDHojalata","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"A Guarda","place":"A Guarda, Spain","at":[41.9029,-8.8564],"text":"Galicia: the hillfort of Santa Trega above the river mouth and a wilder, rockier coast ahead.","by":"ferry","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Location_of_A_Guarda.png/500px-Location_of_A_Guarda.png","page":"A Guarda","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Location_of_A_Guarda.png","credit":"Roi González Villa (Vivaelcelta)","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Baiona","place":"Baiona, Spain","at":[42.0881,-8.8485],"text":"Where the caravel Pinta brought the first news of the Americas in 1493. A walled fortress on the bay.","source":{"label":"Stingy Nomads: coastal stages","url":"https://stingynomads.com/portuguese-coastal-camino-stages/"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Vista_do_porto_de_Baiona_desde_Monterreal-cropped.jpg/500px-Vista_do_porto_de_Baiona_desde_Monterreal-cropped.jpg","page":"Baiona, Pontevedra","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vista_do_porto_de_Baiona_desde_Monterreal-cropped.jpg","credit":"User Alma","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Vigo","place":"Vigo, Spain","at":[42.1986,-8.728],"text":"Spain's busiest fishing port, with the Cíes Islands across the ría."},{"name":"Redondela","place":"Redondela, Spain","at":[42.2799,-8.6163],"text":"Under the railway viaducts the coastal way joins the central Portuguese route: suddenly many more pilgrims."},{"name":"Pontevedra","place":"Pontevedra, Spain","at":[42.4281,-8.6041],"text":"A car-free old town and the scallop-shaped church of the Virgen Peregrina."},{"name":"Caldas de Reis","place":"Caldas de Reis, Spain","at":[42.6183,-8.6614],"text":"A spa town since Roman times: hot springs for tired feet.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Ayuntamiento_001._Caldas_de_Reyes.jpg/500px-Ayuntamiento_001._Caldas_de_Reyes.jpg","page":"Caldas de Reis","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ayuntamiento_001._Caldas_de_Reyes.jpg","credit":"Furado","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Padrón","place":"Padrón, Spain","at":[42.7598,-8.6236],"text":"Where, by legend, the boat carrying Saint James's body landed. Famous for its little green peppers.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Padr%C3%B3n.jpg/500px-Padr%C3%B3n.jpg","page":"Padrón","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Padr%C3%B3n.jpg","credit":"Fran Villena","license":"CC BY 2.0"}},{"name":"Santiago de Compostela","place":"Praza do Obradoiro, Santiago de Compostela","at":[42.8805,-8.5458],"text":"The Obradoiro square and the cathedral: about 280 km from Porto.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Santiago_cathedral_2021.jpg/500px-Santiago_cathedral_2021.jpg","page":"Santiago de Compostela Cathedral","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Santiago_cathedral_2021.jpg","credit":"Fernando","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}}],"legs":[{"by":"walk","km":33,"line":[[41.1429,-8.6112],[41.1483,-8.6372],[41.1481,-8.6749],[41.1669,-8.6882],[41.1874,-8.6924],[41.1908,-8.7056],[41.2047,-8.7156],[41.218,-8.7135],[41.2426,-8.7265],[41.2585,-8.7234],[41.3103,-8.7401],[41.3266,-8.7372],[41.3395,-8.7416],[41.3503,-8.739],[41.354,-8.7435]]},{"by":"walk","km":23,"line":[[41.354,-8.7435],[41.3786,-8.7609],[41.3816,-8.7698],[41.4125,-8.7862],[41.4318,-8.7837],[41.4703,-8.7647],[41.4798,-8.7651],[41.4914,-8.7731],[41.5171,-8.7709],[41.5312,-8.7792]]},{"by":"walk","km":23,"line":[[41.5312,-8.7792],[41.5453,-8.7909],[41.561,-8.7949],[41.5726,-8.7869],[41.5957,-8.791],[41.6302,-8.8194],[41.6518,-8.8247],[41.6679,-8.8191],[41.6826,-8.8325],[41.6935,-8.8284]]},{"by":"walk","km":25,"line":[[41.6935,-8.8284],[41.7043,-8.8024],[41.7311,-8.7804],[41.7647,-8.7837],[41.7742,-8.7725],[41.7943,-8.7777],[41.8134,-8.7658],[41.8176,-8.7686],[41.8193,-8.7644],[41.827,-8.7662],[41.8331,-8.7612],[41.8483,-8.7677],[41.8485,-8.7729]]},{"by":"ferry","km":9,"line":[[41.8492,-8.7727],[41.9029,-8.8564]]},{"by":"walk","km":26,"line":[[41.903,-8.8568],[41.9165,-8.8836],[41.9198,-8.8802],[41.9374,-8.8852],[41.9454,-8.882],[41.9801,-8.8865],[42.0022,-8.8766],[42.0266,-8.8849],[42.0511,-8.8752],[42.0761,-8.8734],[42.0887,-8.849]]},{"by":"walk","km":21,"line":[[42.0887,-8.849],[42.1011,-8.8285],[42.1096,-8.828],[42.115